WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:06.357
In September, Pollyanna started school in Beldingsville.

2
00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:11.221
She quickly made many friends among the boys and girls in her class.

3
00:00:11.222 --> 00:00:15.829
Much to her surprise, she actually enjoyed her schoolwork.

4
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:21.779
Although she was a happy student, she didn't forget her old friends.

5
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.386
She continued to visit Mrs. Snow and Mr. Pendleton on a regular basis.

6
00:00:27.387 --> 00:00:34.573
Mr. Pendleton, however, was not happy and complained to her one Saturday afternoon.

7
00:00:34.574 --> 00:00:39.626
"I rarely see you these days," he said as they sat in his library.

8
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:42.888
"How would you like to come live with me?"

9
00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:45.580
Pollyanna thought he was joking.

10
00:00:45.581 --> 00:00:49.257
"Oh, Mr. Pendleton, you're so funny!

11
00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:53.223
I thought you didn't like having people in your house."

12
00:00:53.224 --> 00:00:57.031
"That was before you taught me to play your wonderful game.

13
00:00:57.032 --> 00:01:00.610
Now I'm glad to have people here to help me.

14
00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:03.032
Not that I'll need them forever.

15
00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.104
I'll soon be up and walking around as usual.

16
00:01:06.105 --> 00:01:11.933
Then, watch out!" He playfully shook one of his crutches at her.

17
00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.687
Pollyanna frowned at him.

18
00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:19.914
"But you aren't really glad about things; you just say you are.

19
00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:23.873
You know, you never play the game the right way."

20
00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:26.923
Mr. Pendleton looked very serious.

21
00:01:26.924 --> 00:01:34.578
"That's why I want you to live with me—to help me play it. So will you come?"

22
00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:39.793
"Mr. Pendleton, you don't really mean that."

23
00:01:39.794 --> 00:01:43.326
"Yes, I do."

24
00:01:43.327 --> 00:01:47.675
When Pollyanna realized he was serious, she felt upset.

25
00:01:47.676 --> 00:01:51.990
"You know I can't. I'm Aunt Polly's!"

26
00:01:51.991 --> 00:01:54.739
He spoke with a sudden fierceness.

27
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.859
"You're no more hers than . . ." His voice grew gentler.

28
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:04.776
"I mean, perhaps she'd allow you to live here. Would you come, if she let you?"

29
00:02:04.777 --> 00:02:10.526
"But Aunt Polly has been so good to me," Pollyanna said slowly.

30
00:02:10.527 --> 00:02:16.642
"She took me in when I didn't have anybody left but the Ladies' Aid and—"

31
00:02:16.643 --> 00:02:21.311
A spasm crossed Mr. Pendleton's face as if he was in pain.

32
00:02:21.312 --> 00:02:27.281
"Pollyanna, a long time ago, I loved somebody very much.

33
00:02:27.282 --> 00:02:30.497
I had hoped to bring her to this house someday.

34
00:02:30.498 --> 00:02:36.832
I imagined how happy we'd be here and that we'd spend the rest of our lives together."

35
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:44.193
"Go on." Pollyanna encouraged him, her eyes full of sympathy. "But

36
00:02:44.194 --> 00:02:48.973
. . . well . . . I didn't bring her here. Never

37
00:02:48.974 --> 00:02:53.177
mind why. I just didn't, that's all." Mr.

38
00:02:53.178 --> 00:02:58.824
Pendleton gazed out the window for a moment before returning his focus to Pollyanna. "Ever

39
00:02:58.825 --> 00:03:05.724
since then, this great, gray pile of stone has been a house but never a home. I

40
00:03:05.725 --> 00:03:10.250
think it takes a spouse's hand and heart to make a house a home. Or

41
00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:14.799
else a child's presence, and I haven't had that either. Now

42
00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:21.604
that you've heard my story, Pollyanna, won't you come and turn this house into a home?" Pollyanna

43
00:03:21.605 --> 00:03:25.938
sprang to her feet, her face bright with joy. "Do

44
00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:31.604
you wish you'd had that woman's hand and heart all this time?" Mr.

45
00:03:31.605 --> 00:03:34.131
Pendleton nodded. "Oh,

46
00:03:34.132 --> 00:03:39.762
I'm so glad!" She sighed contentedly. "You

47
00:03:39.763 --> 00:03:44.359
can take us both, and everything will be all right." "Take

48
00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:49.476
you both?" Mr. Pendleton was puzzled. "Well,

49
00:03:49.477 --> 00:03:52.935
Aunt Polly isn't persuaded yet. But

50
00:03:52.936 --> 00:03:57.894
I'm sure she will be, if you tell your story the same way you told me. Then

51
00:03:57.895 --> 00:04:01.566
we'll both come live with you!" A

52
00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:09.473
look of terror filled Mr. Pendleton's eyes. "Aunt Polly come . . . here ?"

53
00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:15.657
"Unless you'd rather go there? Her house isn't quite as pretty as yours, but it's—"

54
00:04:15.658 --> 00:04:19.046
"Pollyanna, stop! What are you talking about?"

55
00:04:19.047 --> 00:04:22.095
"Where we're going to live, of course."

56
00:04:22.096 --> 00:04:25.905
Surprised by his question, Pollyanna went on.

57
00:04:25.906 --> 00:04:31.991
"You said you wanted Aunt Polly's hand and heart years ago to make a home and—"

58
00:04:31.992 --> 00:04:36.869
A cry came from Mr. Pendleton's throat.

59
00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.547
Before he could speak, the maid suddenly appeared in the doorway.

60
00:04:40.548 --> 00:04:44.484
"Dr. Chilton is here," she announced.

61
00:04:44.485 --> 00:04:46.974
Pollyanna rose to leave.

62
00:04:46.975 --> 00:04:53.398
"Say nothing about what I asked you," Mr. Pendleton begged Pollyanna in a quiet voice.

63
00:04:53.399 --> 00:04:57.187
Pollyanna broke into a grin and called back over her shoulder.

64
00:04:57.188 --> 00:05:02.761
"Of course not. I know you'd rather ask Aunt Polly yourself!"

65
00:05:02.762 --> 00:05:08.524
Mr. Pendleton fell back limply in his chair and tried to breathe calmly.

66
00:05:08.525 --> 00:05:15.773
"What's the matter?" Dr. Chilton rushed to Mr. Pendleton's side and felt his racing pulse.

67
00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:23.898
Mr. Pendleton managed a smile. "Too much of that medicine you prescribed!"

